      "content": "I can't advise you to take both medications without consulting your doctor first. Combining quetiapine with diazepam can increase the risk of severe sedation, respiratory depression, and potentially life-threatening interactions. Please consult your doctor before taking any additional medication, especially if you're experiencing side effects from the quetiapine. \r\n\r\nThat being said, consider the following options to help you get a good night's sleep:\r\n\r\n1. Talk to your doctor about adjusting your quetiapine dosage or adding another medication to complement its effects.\r\n2. Explore other relaxation techniques, such as deep breathing, progressive muscle relaxation, or mindfulness exercises.\r\n3. Create a sleep-conducive environment by ensuring your bedroom is dark, quiet, and at a comfortable temperature.\r\n4. Establish a consistent sleep schedule and routine to help regulate your body's internal clock.\r\n\r\nIf you're experiencing a panic attack tonight, I recommend reaching out to a crisis hotline or a trusted friend or family member for support.",
